# Claude Code machine-local settings, including its transient writes
.claude/settings.local.json*
# Written by the agent as tool approvals accumulate, and full of paths that
# only mean anything inside one session. Shared project settings, if there ever
# are any, want a deliberate commit rather than whatever this happens to hold.
.claude/settings.json

# Reference material dropped in for reading — not part of the app.
input/

# Screenshots from `npm run shots`. Deliberately not committed: they vary with
# the host's fonts and GPU, so diffing them across machines would cry wolf. The
# committed engraving check is the SVG one in src/render/__snapshots__.
shots/

# Review page from `npm run themes`, regenerated on demand.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose. Unanchored, this matches at any depth and
# silently swallowed `public/spike/themes.html`, which is published and must be
# committed — `git add -A` skipped it without a word and CI found it instead.
/themes.html
